        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles John Godfrey Saunders\n- Roles: Bishop of Lucknow\n- Organizations: Merchant Taylors' School, St John’s College Oxford\n- Places: Lucknow, City of London\n- Topics: British independent schools\n\nFacts:\n- Charles John Godfrey Saunders was born in 1884.\n- Charles John Godfrey Saunders was educated at Merchant Taylors' School and at St John’s College, Oxford.\n- From 1928 until 1938, Charles John Godfrey Saunders served as the Bishop of Lucknow.\n- Charles John Godfrey Saunders died on 16 October 1973.\n- Merchant Taylors' School is a British independent private day school for boys.\n- Merchant Taylors' School was originally located in the City of London.",
